WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.398
We have a visible app contract, a real Lovable investigation with permitted
synthetic tools, a specific change stop, and independently correlated Langfuse
evidence.

00:00:09.398 --> 00:00:15.936
We also have alternative-builder frontend comparisons and a local coding route whose
backend limits are explicit.

00:00:15.936 --> 00:00:17.979
These are different acceptance classes.

00:00:17.979 --> 00:00:27.378
We do not let one accepted trace imply that every builder, every persona, OCI APM,
Log Analytics or a cloud deployment has passed.

00:00:27.378 --> 00:00:33.507
The course links each part to the capability it adds and the evidence still
required.

00:00:33.507 --> 00:00:37.184
That clarity is a useful best practice in itself.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:41.077
Keep one OpsDesk project throughout the six parts.

00:00:41.077 --> 00:00:47.336
Save a private baseline reference, launch instructions, selected model, observed
checks and known gaps.

00:00:47.336 --> 00:00:53.148
Repeat create, search, filter, select, investigate and block a change before moving
on.

00:00:53.148 --> 00:01:00.302
Add engine control, model and cost understanding, tracing, security and a reviewed
cloud handoff in sequence.

00:01:00.302 --> 00:01:07.008
GitHub Pages serves the guide and video; it does not run your authenticated AI
backend.

00:01:07.008 --> 00:01:13.268
Pause the film, follow the matching manual task, and continue at your own pace.

00:01:13.268 --> 00:01:19.080
Use synthetic data, keep credentials server-side, and ask what each result actually
proves.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:21.316
Thank you for building along.

00:01:21.625 --> 00:01:30.000
Your turn: follow the manual task. Pause for more time.
